  "text": "<color=@creditsHeader><B>War Thunder</B></color>\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>(c) Gaijin Games KFT</B></color>\n\n\n\nSound recordings by Mats Lundgren and Max Lachmann for Pole Position Production (www.pole.se)\nSpecial thanks to Messerschmitt Foundation, Laura Bonhomme at Old Flying Machine Company, Duxford, UK, Brian Boyer and the guys at Planes of Fame Air Museum, Chino, USA.\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Additional sound recordist</B></color>\n\nJesse Lyon\n\nMain Theme music by Jeremy Soule\n(www.directsong.com)\n\nMusic produced by Gaijin Entertainment\n\nThe soundtrack is recorded on the 1st Radio House Studio in St. Petersburg\nPerformed by Baltic Symphony Orchestra\n\n\nMusic composed, recorded and mixed by Strategic Music\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Executive producer</B></color>\n\nDmitry Kuzmenko\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Composers</B></color>\n\nGeorgy Zheryakov\nZahar Antonov\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Final mix edit</B></color>\n\nGeorgy Zheryakov\nDmitry Kuzmenko\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Conductor</B></color>\n\nMikhail Leontiev\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Sound director</B></color>\n\nAlexey Barashkin\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Additional Music</B></color>\n\nTITLE: Asas Death - Edvard Grieg Op. 46\nPERFORMED BY: David Gosnell\nCOMPOSED BY: David Gosnell (PRS)\nPUBLISHED BY: AudioSparx (ASCAP)\nCOURTESY OF: www.StockMusicSite.com\n\nTITLE: Beethoven - Symphony No.7 (2nd Movement)\nPERFORMED BY: Apollo Symphony Orchestra\nCOMPOSED BY: Ludwig van Beethoven (Public Domain) [50%])\nArranged by Chris Worth (BMI)\nPUBLISHED BY: Perfect Solution Music (BMI)\nCOURTESY OF: www.StockMusicSite.com\n\nTITLE: Ave Verum Corpus\nPERFORMED BY: Apollo Symphony Orchestra\nCOMPOSED BY: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart (Public Domain) [50%])\nArranged by Chris Worth (BMI)\nPUBLISHED BY: Perfect Solution Music (BMI)\nCOURTESY OF: www.StockMusicSite.com\n\nTITLE: Siegfried's Death (From the Ring Cycle)\nPERFORMED BY: Apollo Symphony Orchestra\nCOMPOSED BY: Richard Wagner (Public Domain) [50%])\nArranged by Chris Worth (BMI)\nPUBLISHED BY: Perfect Solution Music (BMI)\nCOURTESY OF: www.StockMusicSite.com\n\nTITLE: Prelude to Act 1 (From Lohengrin)\nPERFORMED BY: Apollo Symphony Orchestra\nCOMPOSED BY: Richard Wagner (Public Domain) [50%])\nArranged by Chris Worth (BMI)\nPUBLISHED BY: Perfect Solution Music (BMI)\nCOURTESY OF: www.StockMusicSite.com\n\nTITLE: Ride of the Valkyries\nPERFORMED BY: Apollo Symphony Orchestra\nCOMPOSED BY: Richard Wagner (Public Domain) [50%])\nArranged by Chris Worth (BMI)\nPUBLISHED BY: Perfect Solution Music (BMI)\nCOURTESY OF: www.StockMusicSite.com\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Special thanks</B></color>\n\nIlya Terentev\nTimofej Cheblokov\nMax Lachmann\nBen Minto\nHugh Edwards\nDmitry Kuzmenko\nJeremy Soule\nJulian Soule\nCity of Saint-Petersburg\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Special thanks</B></color>\n\nFederico Villa (www.gavs.it)\n\nwww.history.navy.mil\nwww.archive.org\nwww.ww2db.com\n\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Alpha Testers lead</B></color>\n\nEugeny 'Skiverrus' Dunaev\n\n<color=@creditsHeader>All who participated in alpha-test:</color>\n\nRuslan 'VerTun' Mametkuliev\nLily '=AxA=_ISIDA' von König\nDenis 'kvigas' Ahmatgaliev\nSergei 'Bulya' Volkov\nAndrey '=axa=_ruNike' Shalakhov\nAntonio 'BG_MAN' Atanasov\nKirill 'Broad_sky' Vostretsov\nTheodor '=PUH=Theo' Nikiporets\nDmitry 'Torion' Vetchinov\nSergey 'Patient' Zagaynov\nVladimir 'ZGame' Gogolevskiy \nAleksey 'D_Idaho' Protzenko\nPavel '=AxA=_OOO' Ryabov\nAlexander 'Kyle' Afonin\nAndrey 'Steel rat' Kuzub\nEugeny 'FW__Raven' Shukevich\nEugeny 'Skiverrus' Dunaev\nAleksandr '=AxA=_KamAL' Kamyhin\nAndrey 'storm62' Tolstoy\nViktor '=PUH=MaV' Makitruk\nAlexander 'SashaSniperUSSR' Rybin\nAlexey '=WF=RAW' Rakcheyev\nVladimir 'DiFiS' Rybin\nDenis 'R_FAZA' Tschumatschenko \nMike 'manuva' Kormilitsyn \nViktor '=HH=Viktor' Sokolov\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Localization</B></color>\n\nQLOC S.A.\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Localization Project Manager</B></color>\n\nAlan Orman\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Additional Localization</B></color>\n\nT57: Localizations & Development\n\n\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Additional Art:</B></color>\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Warlock-games team:</B></color>\n\nAndrey Kuliсk\nDmytro Zosymov\nYefymenko Pavlo\nIhor Kostynenko\nSerhii Holubtsov\nMalitskyi Vadym\nTymoshenko Volodymyr\nKravtsov Maksym\nNikolaenko Natalija\nBorozniak Volodymyr\nPavlo Pirozhenko\nKholkin Eduard\nKhrestin Dmytro\nBratukhin Iurii\nCherniak Oleksandr\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>ArtVostok:</B></color>\n\nAlexey Anoshkin\nDmitry Serkov\nAlexey Klimov\nAlexey Bilibin\nAlexander Shursha\nVladimir Pervykh\nDmitry Poleshchuk\nDmitry Zaregorodzev\nAlena Belousova\nAnna Krotova\nAnna Kvashenko\nStepanenko Aleksej\nAleksandr Kozarezov\nToropov Anton\nDmitry Repp\nRoman Poleshhuk\nDmitry Skripko\nSergej Brauer\nTat'jana Dracheva\nLuckovskij Aleksej\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Art-Std Studio</B></color>\n\nAlexey Durov\nSergey Maksimov\nIvan Skorodmov\nRoman Gluschenko\nPetr Borbishev\nNikolay Aladinskiy\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Heavy Machinery studio:</B></color>\n\nSergey Brauer\nEvgeny Fedotov\nVitaliy Ishkov\nNikolay Konwin\nAnatoly Levkovich\nEgor Guriev\nEmil Mukhtarov\nIlya Mirovich\nIvan Domnar\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Sami Group Studio</B></color>\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Additional graphics</B></color>\n\nMichael 'mikedo' Dorokhin\nSergey 'Losovoy' Lozovoy\nYuriy 'yurezzz' Shemaev\nRoman 'Viper' Smirnov\nAnton 'An-3D' Vorobiev\nOleg 'Neva' Goncharuk-Sukach\nDani Santos\n\n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Additional skins</B></color>\nColin 'Fenris' Muir\nPhilip 'MadMass' D. Massimi \nNeil \"Mysticpuma\" Pugh\nJuan 'vixo' Urizar\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Dagor Engine™ technology </B></color>\n\nCopyright © 2006-2025 Gaijin KFT.\nAll rights reserved. \n\n\n<color=@creditsHeader><B>Northrop Grumman Systems Corporation</B></color>\nXF5F-1 Skyrocket, XP-50, F4F-3 Wildcat, F4F-4 Wi